    "content_html": "<div class=\"articlebodycontent col-xl-9 col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-12\" id=\"content-body-71363219\"><div class=\"schemaDiv\" id=\"schemaDiv\" itemprop=\"articleBody\"><p>The <a href=\"https://www.thehindu.com/tag/204-81/\" target=\"_blank\">Tamil Nadu</a> government on Tuesday (August 18, 2026) suspended M. Ayyasamy, the tahsildar of Guziliamparai in Dindigul district, for ordering Village Assistants and Revenue Inspectors to collect details of members and leaders of the <a href=\"https://www.thehindu.com/topic/communist-party-of-india/\" target=\"_blank\">Communist Party of India (CPI)</a> and <a href=\"https://www.thehindu.com/topic/communist-party-of-india-marxist/\" target=\"_blank\">Communist Party of India (Marxist)</a>. He was directed to appear before the Commissioner of Revenue Administration in Chennai for further inquiry.</p><p>Later, the Dindigul Collector issued an official note stating the Tahsildar’s order was being “immediately withdrawn.”</p><div class=\"article-picture verticle\"><div class=\"picture zoom-img\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"lazy\" data-original=\"https://th-i.thgim.com/public/incoming/mduh5e/article71363533.ece/alternates/FREE_1200/WhatsApp%20Image%202026-08-19%20at%2009.52.12.jpeg\" data-src-template=\"https://th-i.thgim.com/public/incoming/mduh5e/article71363533.ece/alternates/FREE_1200/WhatsApp%20Image%202026-08-19%20at%2009.52.12.jpeg\" height=\"100%\" src=\"https://www.thehindu.com/theme/images/th-online/1x1_spacer.png\" width=\"100%\"/></div><span itemprop=\"image\" itemscope=\"itemscope\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/ImageObject\"></span><meta content=\"https://th-i.thgim.com/public/incoming/mduh5e/article71363533.ece/alternates/FREE_1200/WhatsApp%20Image%202026-08-19%20at%2009.52.12.jpeg\" itemprop=\"url\"/><meta content=\"1200\" itemprop=\"width\"/><meta content=\"675\" itemprop=\"height\"/></div><p>“We do not know why he [the Tahsildar] issued the orders. But I was told that he has been suspended, and the reasons behind his order will be known only after the inquiry,” said CPI(M) State secretary P. Shanmugam.</p><p>Mr. Ayyasamy issued the order on August 18 and directed officials to submit the details by the evening. “Otherwise, action will be taken against Village Assistants,” his order said.</p><p>Commenting on the order on social media, CPI(M) MP Sachithanandam said such an order had not been issued even when political parties were banned and the Criminal Tribes Act was in force.</p></div><div class=\"articleblock-container\" id=\"arthardpv\"></div><div class=\"update-publish-time article-published-time-end\"><p class=\"publish-time-new\"> Published <span>- August 19, 2026 08:51 am IST</span></p></div><div class=\"comments-shares share-page flex print-hide\" data-artid=\"71363219\" data-title=\"Tahsildar in Dindigul suspended for ordering collection of CPI, CPI(M) members’ details\" data-url=\"https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/tamil-nadu/in-tn-tahsildar-suspended-for-ordering-collection-of-details-of-communist-party-members/article71363219.ece\"><div class=\"left\"><div class=\"share\"><button class=\"btn share-btn\" data-ga-labelclick=\"ArticleShare\"></button><ul class=\"share-list bottom\" style=\"display: none;\"><li class=\"copy-link\" data-cf-modified-fd476134c9bef812bac21d27-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; copytext('https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/tamil-nadu/in-tn-tahsildar-suspended-for-ordering-collection-of-details-of-communist-party-members/article71363219.ece');\">\n                Copy link  \n                        \n            </li><li class=\"email\"><a href=\"mailto:?subject=Tahsildar%20in%20Dindigul%20suspended%20for%20ordering%20collection%20of%20CPI%2C%20CPI%28M%29%20members%E2%80%99%20details&amp;amp;body=Check%20out%20this%20link%20https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thehindu.com%2Fnews%2Fnational%2Ftamil-nadu%2Fin-tn-tahsildar-suspended-for-ordering-collection-of-details-of-communist-party-members%2Farticl